# File spec for ./test.rs. The dispatcher, the log line and the exit-3 trap belong to
# ./mod.sdd. The engine lives under ./../testing/ (its specs are pending); it is named
# as collaborator here, never restated.

Spec: PackageTest

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  The `agent package test` leaf — the offline, mock-only test-suite runner for a package
    directory: gate `<package_dir>/tests`, build one @client::testing::TestHandler from the
    four CLI directories plus one optional extra testset directory, then either print the
    loaded test names (default), run the whole suite (`--all`) or one named test
    (`--test-name`) through the engine's mocked Rhai interpreter (kubernetes-mock and
    http-mock only — no cluster, no kind, no live API), print the summary in `text` or
    `json`, optionally write a JUnit XML file and, for a single test only, dump the
    objects the mock layer recorded as multi-document YAML, and fold every failing
    assertion into one @Err @common::Error::TestFailure that ./mod.sdd traps as exit 3.
  The `client::` import prefix is the agent crate's own library name (`[lib] name = "client"`
    in /agent/Cargo.toml); @TestHandler resolves to ./../testing/handler.rs inside this crate.

Owns:
  ./test.rs

References:
  ./mod.sdd — caller and exit lane: any @Err from @run is Display-logged
    `Testing the package failed with: {e:}` via @tracing::error! then
    @std::process::exit(3); this file itself neither logs nor exits.
  ./../testing/mod.sdd, ./../testing/handler.sdd, ./../testing/result.sdd,
    ./../testing/vyniltest.sdd, ./../testing/vyniltestset.sdd — the engine this leaf
    drives; every one pending — cross-reference only, their behaviour is owned there.
  /common/src/lib.sdd — @common::Error / @common::Result contract: @Error::MissingTestDirectory,
    @Error::TestFailure, @Error::Stdio, @Error::YamlError and @Error::Core's transparent
    wrap of `vynil-core` errors.
  /common/src/yamlhandler.sdd — @yaml_all_serialize_to_string, the `vynil-core` `0.7.7`
    multi-document YAML serializer used by the template-output dump.
  /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd — @Dynamic, the value type the created-object sink carries.
  /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — @read_package_yaml and the package-type inference the
    engine performs from `package.yaml` (this CLI carries no package-type flag).
  /docs/cli.md — the documented `agent package test` synopsis and `MissingTestDirectory`
    error notice the parent /agent/agent.sdd pins stable.

Must:
  Freeze the ten-argument clap surface exactly: `-p`/`--package-dir`/env `PACKAGE_DIRECTORY`
    default `/tmp/package`; `-s`/`--script-dir`/env `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY` default
    `./agent/scripts`; `-t`/`--template-dir`/env `TEMPLATE_DIRECTORY` default
    `./agent/templates`; `-c`/`--config-dir`/env `CONFIG_DIR` default `.`;
    `--testsets-dir` (no short)/env `TESTSETS_DIRECTORY`, optional @PathBuf, Rust field
    @testset_dir; `--test-name`/env `TEST_NAME`, optional @String; `--all` boolean flag
    with no short form and no env; `--format`, no env, `default_value = "text"`;
    `--junit-output-filename` (no short)/env `JUNIT_OUTPUT_FILENAME`, optional @PathBuf;
    `--template-output-filename` (no short)/env `TEMPLATE_OUTPUT_FILENAME`, optional
    @PathBuf whose doc text reads `Template output filename (only available for a single
    test)`. Every env-bound arg's value name equals its env name; resolution order is flag
    over env over default; the relative defaults `./agent/scripts`, `./agent/templates`
    and `.` bind against the process cwd at use time.
  Accept under @format exactly `text` and `json` (the @clap::ValueEnum names, exact case;
    the enum derives no @Default — the arg's `default_value` string arms the default), and
    @format_results maps @OutputFormat::Json to @TestResultCollector::to_json and
    @OutputFormat::Text to @TestResultCollector::to_text.
  Gate everything before any load: @PathBuf::join("tests") of @package_dir must
    @Path::is_dir — the directory is never created here — otherwise @Err
    @Error::MissingTestDirectory carrying @package_dir itself, whose display
    `Missing tests directory {0}` therefore names the package directory, not the
    `<package_dir>/tests` path the gate actually checked.
  Build the engine exactly once with @TestHandler::new(package_dir, script_dir,
    config_dir, template_dir, @testset_dir wrapped in a one-element @Vec) — at most one
    extra testset directory reaches the engine — and propagate every constructor @Err with
    `?`: load of `<package_dir>/package.yaml`, the non-recursive `.yml`/`.yaml` file scan
    of the extra testset directory (TestSet documents only) and of `<package_dir>/tests`
    (Test and TestSet documents, selected by apiVersion `vinyl.solidite.fr/v1beta1` —
    literal `vinyl` spelling — plus kind), and duplicate Test/TestSet names all abort in
    the exit-3 trap before a summary line or a test name prints, in every mode including
    list mode.
  Select the mode at frozen precedence: `--all` over `--test-name` (both set runs the
    whole suite and the name is silently ignored); neither set selects list mode, which
    @println!s one @TestHandler::list_tests name per line in the engine's sorted order and
    returns @Ok early — the summary, the verdict, junit and template lanes never run.
  Run the all lane through @TestHandler::run_all_tests: engine order is ascending test-name
    order (BTreeMap key order), each test gets its own fresh created-object sink that
    never reaches this file, so `--template-output-filename` cannot be served here and is
    silently ignored; then @println! @format_results and write `@to_junit` when
    `--junit-output-filename` is set.
  Run the single lane with a fresh @Arc<Mutex<Vec<Dynamic>>> sink handed to
    @TestHandler::run_test(@test_name, &sink) as the sole channel through which the
    mocked kubernetes layer returns the objects a test created; then print the summary,
    write junit if requested, and when `--template-output-filename` is set lock the sink
    recovering poison via @PoisonError::into_inner, @clone the vec, serialize the whole
    list through @yaml_all_serialize_to_string — yielding one `---` document per object,
    or an empty string for an empty sink — and @std::fs::write it (a run that creates no
    objects leaves a zero-byte file).
  Aggregate the verdict last, after the summary printed and every requested artifact
    wrote: @TestResultCollector::all_passed false yields @Err
    @Error::TestFailure(@total_failed, @total_asserts) — both arguments are assertion
    counts — whose display `Tests failed: {0} failed out of {1} assertions` becomes the
    body of ./mod.sdd's exit-3 line; engine-side errors never @Err out of
    @run_test/@run_all_tests (both return `()` and record an internal failure as failed
    assertions), so a failing suite leaves exactly this one synthetic @Err with summary
    and artifacts already emitted.
  Keep the posture mock and file-only: this file opens no kube client, never calls
    @common::context::init_k8s, provisions no kind or live cluster, and takes all state
    from files resolved by the engine directories; the created-object sink is the only
    per-test state it sees or injects.
  Write through exactly two channels — @println! to stdout for the summary and list mode —
    and @std::fs::write (truncate-or-create, silent overwrite of existing files, parent
    directories never created) for artifacts; allocate no temp directory and delete
    nothing: artifacts written before a later @Err survive on disk.

Must not:
  Log its own failure or call @std::process::exit — the Display trap and exit 3 are
    ./mod.sdd's; error identity here travels only inside @common::Error.
  Abort the suite on the first failing assertion — every selected test runs to the end,
    the summary and artifacts flush, and only then does the single aggregated @Err fire.
  Reject an unknown `--test-name` as a usage error — it reaches the engine and comes back
    as one failed `execution` assertion, not a @Err before the run.
  Let @format touch anything but the stdout summary — the JUnit file is always `@to_junit`
    XML and list mode always plain names, whatever `--format` says.

Exposes:
  @Parameters — `#[derive(@clap::Args, @Debug, @Serialize, @Deserialize)]` with ten
    private fields (@package_dir, @script_dir, @template_dir, @config_dir, @testset_dir,
    @test_name, @start_all behind `--all`, @format, @junit_output_filename,
    @template_output_filename); outside this module they are reached only through
    @Commands::Test in ./mod.rs.
  @run — `pub fn @run(args: &@Parameters) -> @common::Result<@()>`; synchronous, sync
    called by ./mod.sdd's exit-3 arm, awaited by nobody.
  @OutputFormat — `pub enum` @Text/`@Json` with `#[value(name = "text")]`/
    `#[value(name = "json")]` and `#[serde(rename_all = "snake_case")]`.
  @PackageType — `pub enum` @Tenant/@Service/@System (default @System) deriving
    @clap::ValueEnum, @Default and serde snake_case; nothing in @Parameters or anywhere
    else in the crate references it (dead — Tasks).
  All four are module-boundary public only: `mod test;` in ./mod.rs is private, so the
    crate surface exports none of them.

Accepts:
  A clap-parsed @Parameters by reference; the only existence check before parsing work is
    the tests-directory gate — every @PathBuf is otherwise taken unvalidated.
  Environment fallbacks for every env-bound argument while its flag is absent.
  @test_name as an exact string matched against loaded Test names by the engine — no
    pattern, glob or case-insensitive lane here.

Returns:
  @Ok(()) after list mode prints its names (even zero of them), or after a run whose every
    assert passed — an empty suite vacuously qualifies.
  @Err — always ./mod.sdd's exit-3 trap; see Raises.

Raises:
  @Error::MissingTestDirectory(@std::path::PathBuf) — tests-directory gate, payload is
    @package_dir (see Must).
  Constructor @Errs propagated verbatim from @TestHandler::new (owned by
    ./../testing/handler.sdd, pending): scan I/O as @Error::Stdio, unparseable documents
    and duplicate Test/TestSet names as @Error::YamlError with `{file}: ` prefixed
    messages, plus the @package.yaml read leg of /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd.
  @Error::Stdio(@std::io::Error) — junit or template @std::fs::write failure (missing
    parent directory first among them); on the single lane a junit failure skips the
    template write and the verdict check alike.
  @Error::Core over `vynil-core` @Error::YamlError — @yaml_all_serialize_to_string refusing
    a recorded @Dynamic @serde_yaml cannot render.
  @Error::TestFailure(@usize, @usize) — the aggregated verdict; failing individual tests
    never surface as their own @Err.
  No panic is expected from this file's code: the sink lock is poison-recovered, not
    unwrapped; anything the engine panics on is outside this contract.

Handles:
  `tests` present but not a directory — same gate @Err as absent, no distinct branch.
  Empty suite directory — list mode prints nothing and @Ok's; `--all` runs zero tests,
    prints the zero-tally text summary, vacuously passes and exits 0.
  Unknown @test_name — the summary shows a failing `execution` assert reading
    `Test '<name>' not found`, then @Error::TestFailure(1, 1) drives exit 3.
  Poisoned created-object lock — recovered through @PoisonError::into_inner, the value is
    still dumped.
  `--all` together with `--test-name` and `--template-output-filename` — all lane runs,
    the name and the template file are silently ignored, no warning prints.
  JUnit and template both set on the single lane — junit writes first; a subsequent
    verdict @Err leaves both files on disk.
  Duplicate TestSet name between the extra testset directory and the suite directory —
    both merge into one engine map, so the collision @Err's construction and kills the
    command pre-output.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover @run with tests — no #[cfg(test)] module exists in this file, nothing under
      /agent/tests drives `agent package test`, and the only in-tree tests nearby sit in
      ./../testing/result.rs; map each scenario to a same-named test: suite-gate-before-load,
      default-mode-lists-plain-names, green-suite-exits-ok, failing-suite-prints-then-errs,
      unknown-test-name-is-one-failed-assert, template-dump-is-multidoc-yaml with
      template-dump-empty-suite-writes-zero-byte-file, all-wins-over-test-name-and-drops-template-file,
      junit-write-error-preempts-verdict, empty-suite-exits-zero.
  [?] @PackageType is dead code — defined `pub` (Tenant/Service/System, default System) but
      referenced by nothing here or in the crate; the package kind is inferred from
      `package.yaml` by the engine. Decide to delete it or wire a real package-type flag.
  [?] @OutputFormat exists twice in sibling modules — this file and ./lint.rs define
      identical text/json enums independently. Decide whether one shared type serves both
      leaves.
  [?] `--template-output-filename` with `--all` is silently ignored although its help text
      claims single-test scope, and @TestHandler::run_all_tests hides a per-test sink so no
      all-run could ever answer it. Decide: reject the combination, or freeze silent
      ignore in documentation.
  [?] @TestHandler::validate_refs is never called from this leaf, so a Test referencing an
      unknown TestSet lists and prints fine, then fails only as a per-test `execution`
      assert. Decide whether list or load should pre-validate references.
  [?] @Error::MissingTestDirectory carries @package_dir while the gate checked
      `<package_dir>/tests`, so the exit-3 line can read `Missing tests directory
      /tmp/package` — the exact missing path is never echoed. Decide the payload convention.

Done when:
  Every scenario carries a mapped passing test, the `[?]` decisions above are recorded, and
    `cargo test -p agent`, clippy and `cargo +nightly fmt --check` stay green.

Scenario: suite gate fires before any load
  Given `-p /pkg` where `/pkg/tests` is absent or is a regular file
  When @run runs
  Then @Err @Error::MissingTestDirectory("/pkg") returns before @package.yaml is read,
    @TestHandler::new runs or anything prints
  And ./mod.sdd logs `Testing the package failed with: Missing tests directory /pkg` and
    exits 3
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: default mode lists plain names
  Given a loaded suite and no `--all` and no `--test-name` (even `--format json`, even a
    suite whose Tests reference an unknown TestSet)
  When @run runs
  Then each test name `@println!`s alone on its line, in sorted order, no summary line
    prints, no artifact file is written
  And @Ok returns and exit 0 follows whatever the verdict would be
  A missing or unparseable `package.yaml` still errors here — build precedes listing.
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: green suite prints summary and exits 0
  Given `--all` over a suite whose asserts all pass
  When @run runs
  Then the `--format`-rendered summary (`text` blocks plus `Results: N passed, 0 failed,
    N total`, or the `json` object) prints to stdout
  And `--junit-output-filename` when given writes `@to_junit` XML with one suite per test
  And @Ok returns; exit 0
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: failing suite prints, artifacts flush, then one aggregated Err
  Given `--all junit/template output` where some asserts fail
  When @run runs
  Then the full FAIL summary prints, the junit file exists on disk afterwards
  And @Err @Error::TestFailure counts failed assertions over total assertions — `Tests
    failed: 2 failed out of 5 assertions` — and exit 3 follows
  But no engine-internal error ever reaches @Err — a test whose scripts crash still just
    contributes failed asserts
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: unknown test name dies as a test, not as usage
  Given `--test-name nope` over a loaded suite lacking it
  When @run runs
  Then the summary shows test `nope` with a failing `execution` assert reading
    `Test 'nope' not found`
  And @Err @Error::TestFailure(1, 1) exits 3 — clap accepted the name and no early
    rejection happened
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: single-test template dump is multi-document YAML
  Given one `--test-name` run recording two created objects and
    `--template-output-filename /out/dump.yaml`
  When @run runs
  Then `/out/dump.yaml` holds the two objects, each led by a `---` document marker, in
    sink order
  But Given a passing run that creates no objects — the file exists and is empty
  And a missing `/out` directory fails as @Error::Stdio before the verdict check
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: all wins over name and drops the template lane
  Given `--all --test-name one --template-output-filename /dump.yaml`
  When @run runs
  Then every test runs (not just `one`), no `/dump.yaml` is ever written, no warning
    prints
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: empty suite vacuously passes
  Given `<package_dir>/tests` existing but holding no matching documents, `--all`
  When @run runs
  Then stdout is exactly the zero tally `Results: 0 passed, 0 failed, 0 total` (plus
    summary framing)
  And @Ok returns and exit 0
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: junit write failure preempts the verdict
  Given a green-intent suite with `--junit-output-filename /nodir/report.xml` whose writes
    fail as @Error::Stdio
  When @run runs
  Then @Err @Error::Stdio returns from the write — the all-passed verdict check is not
    reached — and exit 3 prints `Testing the package failed with: Stdio error …`
  No mapped test exists.
